KZ3 patch 2059 (RSX pass 59): an A8R8G8B8 read of a Z24S8 zeta address gets the depth byte rebuild in its shader
only when the bind really takes the zeta.
Cause of the pause-screen blur's black blocky holes and of the orange wash / red blocks over the main menu after
Pause > Quit: KZ3's 320x180 blur ping-pong (0x2980000, 0x2DA0000; downsample of 0x1300000, two 4-tap blur passes,
SET_SHADER_PACKER 1, gamma on R,G,B) shares its addresses with the level's shadow-map zetas. Patch 2044 decides at
the bind which one an A8R8G8B8 read takes (the zeta only when its depth is newer than the last real colour write),
but get_pso tagged every such unit ZALIAS_ARGB from tex_zalias_kind alone, so the pixel shader ran
rsx_fp_apply_depth_argb (patch 2011) on the colour texel: .x taken as depth and split into A,R,G bytes, and no gamma
decode. Measured (LD_DRAW_INPUTS dumps, draws 72-75 of a menu frame): fresh boot the blur keeps (1,0,1)/255 through
both passes; after a quit the same draws give 13/255 then 64/255 (rebuilt bytes, then sRGB-encoded twice), the
composite adds that as an orange layer; in the level the same passes punch holes where the rebuilt bytes saturate.
rsx_live_draw.c: ld_argb_zeta_pref (2044's rule, shared by the bind and the PSO) and ld_shader_zalias_kind (ZALIAS_ARGB
only when the zeta is preferred or no colour surface, the draw's own target included, sits at the address); used for
get_pso's per-unit kind (argb_mask, gamma) and for patch 2021's unnormalised-size rule. LD_NO_ARGB_BIND_MATCH=1 = old
tagging. Log: [zeta-argb] ... pso unit reads colour (first 16). Host test tools/smoke/test_zeta_argb.c case D now
checks all four channels of a 0.3 colour (COL0 = 1 survived the rebuild by accident). Upstream candidate (general
aliasing rule, follows 2011/2044).

